Description: a fullscreen window on top keeps the keyboard focus
 labwc focuses every view that becomes visible. thinfloe-menu, the desktop,
 is always-on-bottom and replaces its window whenever its monitor changes,
 for example when a monitor wakes from power save. The new menu window then
 took the keyboard focus from the fullscreen ThinLinc session that still
 covered it: keys went to the hidden menu, where Tab and Enter could reach
 the Restart tile.
 .
 A view that becomes visible is no longer focused when it is
 always-on-bottom and the topmost view of the workspace is fullscreen and
 holds the focus. Such a view can never be raised above the fullscreen
 view, so the focus stays with the window the user sees. Any other new view
 is focused as before, and a click still focuses the always-on-bottom view.
 .
 For this test to see the view's place in the stack, the first-map window
 rules (here ToggleAlwaysOnBottom) now run before the view becomes visible
 and is focused. Before, a new view was raised and focused first and only
 then sent to the bottom.
 .
 thinfloe-specific: not proposed for upstream inclusion, see Forwarded below.
Author: ThinFloe maintainers
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-12
